"Support for these ESCs is included in Copter-4.0 (and higher), Plane-3.10 "
"(and higher) and Rover-3.5 (and higher)"
msgstr "Copter-4.0（及更高版本）、Plane-3.10（及更高版本）和 Rover-3.5（及更高版本）支持这些电调"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:26
#: 69c021926a2c49b2b31e5d76fdcb85bb 8b3a50a96d34472094dfc09d948f3940
#: baf4a120c6ee47b681920e7025415534 c37159b84c0d4facb9a2ade35be34e5b
msgid "Where To Buy"
msgstr "购买渠道"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:28
#: 9d33916110094f09b4c3a1ec92fd52de c5666f1be6274a2ba4f813258ee79e7b
#: d9a08d7fbdf642e9b2d08f312978a153 ed21b8a79a3e4b0da445b0a1d533cc3b
msgid ""
"These ESCs can be purchased by directly contacting the following companies "
"(replace \"AT\" with \"@\" in the email addresses)"
msgstr "这些电调可直接联系以下公司购买（将邮件地址中的「AT」替换为「@」）"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:30
#: aa44a93336294863825627d58a2c0343 bc57e669d9dc40dd81a1fa82d05bd1df
#: d13cd6f5293d463c90f113e83b3de720 f5741c0c15f546dbae918812292667c3
msgid "Toshiba USA: Alan.Li AT taec.toshiba.com"
msgstr "Toshiba 美国：Alan.Li AT taec.toshiba.com"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:31
#: 3480b8c5f9ab4b9c8c8e42b26ca5fe4f 56de8e6621384c1aa56fc42b155256a8
#: e298e50abeb84a48a06a556797bdb91b fec96773abdd47bea75a3d82ff5b37b0
msgid "Hikari Alphax Japan: masaki_nakamura AT h-ax.com"
msgstr "Hikari Alphax 日本：masaki_nakamura AT h-ax.com"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:33
#: 3f24d70b4e8f4f55855a2c597ed1ccf3 4849789c1249417aaf1cbf558437c475
#: 61e2747b19154635a5e34a48663b6ac6 f70fdc1c47a741cbb83ff214ca7c416b
msgid ""
"CAN splitter boards are also required, the boards used in the above video "
"were provided by `EAMS Lab <http://elab.co.jp/>`__ but these are also not "
"readily available for sale."
msgstr ""
"还需要 CAN 分线板，上述视频中使用的分线板由 `EAMS Lab <http://elab.co.jp/>`__ 提供，但这些板子也无法轻易购买到。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:36
#: 3468960cb8804b9eaf8b8efadedcc39a 3d0450c6b33e4727a8a1390d165f9b67
#: e1eca77532404f3197478c760aae9873 f28d591901a748d69a8ccaaccc7d3015
msgid "Connection and Configuration"
msgstr "连接与配置"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:42
#: 08f544d5252d457099806eab9606391c 1b8aa1a9b4554f6a9c99824c73e359fd
#: 4e70cf5fe44241cda7ff85e878c28e43 c211ce5573f2491c8ceb9a1f281f880b
msgid ""
"ESCs should be daisy chained together using CAN splitter boards and then one"
" 4-pin CAN cable should be connected to the autopilot's CAN port.  Note that"
" the last splitter board has a terminator (i.e. no port) on one side."
msgstr ""
"电调应通过 CAN 分线板串联连接，然后用一根 4 芯 CAN 线连接到飞控的 CAN 端口。注意最后一个分线板的一侧有终端电阻（即无端口）。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:46
#: 18f9304d4ca740c0b78f4aa4e9944c34 5b873f5d67a74f99b997d0253a2ba270
#: 9b59c31e9f774932b1ed4080169e051e dd46651c301546f9b0a56d6d23cb2a6a
msgid ""
"If using a Cube autopilot, the CAN1 and CAN2 labels are reversed.  These "
"instructions assume the ESCs are connected to the CAN1 port which is "
"labelled \"CAN2\" on Cube autopilots"
msgstr ""
"如果使用 Cube 飞控，CAN1 和 CAN2 标签是反的。这些说明假设电调连接到 CAN1 端口，在 Cube 飞控上标注为「CAN2」"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:52
#: 1eeda844f00d4eed9a41c48c20f04200 40a5a544819245759ad4fe0b23ffef4c
#: a36a6d8e015d4644ae105a7d9a7e9910 c55e583ebad14b0986753a25571f17da
msgid ""
"Set the dip switches on each ESC to specify its unique number.  This number "
"also maps the ESC to an equivalent PWM output on the back of the autopilot."
"  For example ESC 1 will react just like a normal PWM ESC connected to the "
"autopilot's MAIN OUT 1.  By default this mapping also matches the "
":ref:`motor order diagrams <Copter:connect-escs-and-motors>`."
msgstr ""
"在每个电调上设置拨码开关以指定其唯一编号。该编号同时将电调映射到飞控背面对应的 PWM 输出。例如，电调 1 的响应与连接到飞控 MAIN OUT 1 "
"的普通 PWM 电调相同。默认情况下，此映射也与 :ref:`电机顺序图 <Copter:connect-escs-and-motors>` 匹配。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:53
#: 89a11ae7a6e342f2bd555314540f97c8 89eb9fef65b84292ad2cc94fb50d323c
#: c5f1e7c57a9847948df9e48f419ff444 e18c56d9eb3d44bab8b808e1d1e243b0
msgid "Set :ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL <CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 3 (ToshibaCAN)"
msgstr "设置 :ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL <CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 3（ToshibaCAN）"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:54
#: 467b7388869d4bdfaa146bb2227e8ca7 95ac0fb2560745bbba93fac68e1ac09b
#: d651e4f373b64e61ab0ef66ccc358a65 eafb19f9337849a88a4abb6fa858c71e
msgid ""
"Set :ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER <CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1 (First driver) to specify that "
"the ESCs are connected to the CAN1 port"
msgstr ""
"设置 :ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER <CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1（第一驱动器），以指定 ESC 连接到 CAN1 端口"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:56
#: 285f48f9873e4c04afdc4b958542fe8c a11f5ce76f0e4b5eb372160ec875470d
msgid ""
"Set :ref:`MOT_PWM_MIN <MOT_PWM_MIN>` = 1000 and :ref:`MOT_PWM_MAX "
"<MOT_PWM_MAX>` = 2000 so ArduPilot uses an output range that matches the "
"ESCs input range"
msgstr ""
"设置 :ref:`MOT_PWM_MIN <MOT_PWM_MIN>` = 1000 以及 :ref:`MOT_PWM_MAX "
"<MOT_PWM_MAX>` = 2000，使 ArduPilot 使用与 ESC 输入范围匹配的输出范围"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:59
#: 420ba199d0584fe58d5a30a67dddd106
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"Set :ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>` = 0.03 meaning the motors will spin "
"at 3% of full thrust when armed"
msgstr "设置 :ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>` = 0.03，表示解锁时电机将以最大推力的 3% 转速旋转"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:60
#: 53fc0bb8b12549cf8cf63b9b92bd71bd
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"Set :ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>` = 0.05 meaning the motors will spin "
"at no less than 5% of full thrust when flying"
msgstr "设置 :ref:`MOT_SPIN_MIN <MOT_SPIN_MIN>` = 0.05，表示飞行时电机转速不低于最大推力的 5%"

#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:60
#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:62
#: ../../source/docs/common-toshiba-can-escs.rst:65
#: 32a25016dc4846c789651abcf483dbf2 a3f001145e5c4ce3b1ff4e2a2ca10567
#: a56033461b1a40619d200f20eef342fd be4cab41accc4b5ca94a210a93ca7882
msgid "Logging and Reporting"
